  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe low pressure system that moves through at the beginning of the \nweek will drop our temperatures, but only by about 10 degrees. \nThough, it will bring them closer to average for this time of year \nwith highs in the 60s and lows in the 40s for the rest of the week. \nCloud cover starts to dissipate on Wednesday and skies remain partly \ncloudy to mostly sunny into the weekend. Rain chances have returned \nback into the forecast this Thursday as another low pressure system \nmoves through. Model guidance has struggled with these rain chances, \nbut we'll take the rain if we can get it. Rain chances are 40-60% \nthrough the day Thursday with the higher chances occurring over the \nwestern CWA. Surface high pressure moves back in for the weekend. \nDry weather is expected and patchy fog may occur if lows can dip \ninto the 30s this weekend.",
